Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

t_01a1d59d3ef805c4, design t_01a1d563324d7e8e §2 P2/§9, review R7/R8.

What:
- kanban_activity_revision: every bumping trigger (epoch 2, marked /* kanban-activity-epoch:2 */) also upserts
  kanban_task_change(task_id PK, rev) WITHOUT ROWID, indexed on rev, with the revision it bumped to. Keys: tasks.id,
  both task_links ends, task_id elsewhere; UPDATE marks OLD and NEW when the key moves; DELETE marks OLD; INSERT OR
  REPLACE is covered by the INSERT upsert. A (re)install bumps and upserts FULL_MARK ('').
- Same exclusions as the board revision (R8): bookkeeping columns and heartbeat events do not bump or mark. Fixes a
  hole found while testing: on a synced board the sync insert trigger's own uid stamp (UPDATE task_events SET uid ...
  WHERE uid IS NULL) re-bumped every heartbeat event; a NULL->value uid stamp no longer counts (SYNC_STAMPED).
- SHADOW_TABLES widened to tasks, task_links, task_runs, task_events, task_comments, task_chat_links (R8).
- ensure_revision: leaves the whole trigger set alone when any trigger is of a newer epoch (no drop of unknown
  PREFIX* triggers); repairs a missing change table/index.
- New kanban_task_change.changed_since(conn, cursor) -> (frozenset | FULL, cursor'). Trusted only when (in one
  snapshot): every watched table carries epoch>=2 triggers and the change table exists; (a) MAX(rev) == revision;
  (b) revision >= cursor's; (c) (dev, ino), -shm identity and schema_version equal the cursor's; no FULL_MARK newer
  than the cursor; identity unchanged after the read. Otherwise FULL (with a fresh cursor when the file vouches).
- scripts/benchmark_kanban_task_change.py.

Proof:
- RED: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_task_change.py against origin/main's trigger generation/ensure_revision/
  SHADOW_TABLES: 18/18 failed. GREEN: 25 passed.
- Mutants (sdlc-review mutants.py, 19 by exact anchor over both modules): 19/19 killed.
- Focused suites: 26 files / 447 passed (activity, chat links, replica, sync repair, schema owner, session
  activity, board read/rows caches); 63 files / 1562 passed (sync, db_sync, watcher, idle, notify, incremental,
  content key). test_kanban_schema_owner excludes kanban_task_change from the at-par reference, like the revision.
- Write overhead (committed bumping write, 12x200 alternating blocks, same file): 3747.7 us bump-only vs 3773.7 us
  bump+mark = +0.69% (<= 5%). Statement-only CPU (no commit): 3.85 -> 8.74 us/UPDATE (+4.9 us).
- Scale: changed_since for one touched task at 1k / 5.8k / 20k tasks = 93.8 / 96.8 / 97.8 us (20k/1k = 1.04x,
  <= 1.5x); a full tasks read is 4.4 / 26.9 / 89.7 ms.
- Hub shadow rate (10 min, 2 s windows): windows where a local-or-shadow revision moves 114 -> 139 of 296 once
  runs/events are watched; union with the hub replica 181 -> 197. This is the R8 trade: readers that key on the shadow
  revision refresh more often, and changed_since lets them refresh only the touched tasks (cards E/F).
